    <item>
      <title>The Gluttony of King Nahusha</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In ancient India, King Nahusha, a great warrior and just ruler, was chosen as the new king of the Nishadas. As he sat on his throne, he saw a beautiful Apsara, Alambusha, who had been cursed by the gods for her vanity. Nahusha, being a man of great strength and power, decided to take Alambusha as his queen. He was immediately smitten with her and became obsessed with her. He spent all his days and nights with her, giving her the finest clothes, ornaments, and food. He forgot about his kingdom, his people, and his duties as a king. His gluttony for Alambusha&apos;s beauty and company consumed him. He became a shadow of his former self, a man who had once been a great warrior and a just ruler. Alambusha, seeing Nahusha&apos;s obsession, began to play a cruel trick on him. She would dress up as a lowly servant girl and Nahusha, blinded by his love, would give her the finest clothes and jewels. He would throw lavish feasts for her, forgetting about his people&apos;s struggles. His people suffered, his kingdom fell into chaos, and Nahusha&apos;s downfall was complete. This is Gluttony — the excessive desire for something that consumes you, leaving you empty and hollow.</description>
